      "writtenOn": "2022-07-06T21:54:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your way of handling the endianness will not work.\ne.g.\n```\nbig_endian_packets;\nstruct LotsOfBitfields {\n   a: 1,\n   b: 6, // offset 7\n   c: 2, // offset 9\n   d: 6, // offset 15\n   e: 1, // offset 16\n};\n```\n\nThe documented way of parsing this is:\n```\nlet a \u003d from_big_endian(buf[0..2]) \u0026 0x1;\nlet b \u003d (from_big_endian(buf[0..2]) \u003e\u003e 1) \u0026 0x7f;\n..\n```\nBy taking the fields one by one, you would get:\n```\nlet a \u003d from_big_endian(buf[0..1]) \u0026 0x1;\nlet b \u003d (from_big_endian(buf[0..1]) \u003e\u003e 1) \u0026 0x7f;\n..\n```\ni.e. `a` and `b` are parsed from the wrong byte.\nThe same remark applies for the field serialization.",
      "revId": "82b6b949ab06441da92937728369e98bc630dd8c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
